expo-widgets 58.0.19 (Android): the custom-notification sources published on
the sdk-58 branch import Peek under `io.github.jakex7.peek.*`, while the
package's own Gradle dependency is `io.github.expo.peek:peek-emittables:0.3.2`,
whose artifacts (and the transitive peek-notification 0.3.2) ship their
classes under `io.github.expo.peek.*`. `:expo-widgets:compileDebugKotlin`
therefore fails with "Unresolved reference 'jakex7'" on every build that
autolinks expo-widgets on Android. expo main fixed the imports in
expo/expo#51654 ("[expo-widgets] Fix the Android build of custom
notifications", 2026-10-16); this patch is that rename, nothing else.

Remove this patch when the app moves to an expo-widgets release that
contains expo/expo#51654.

diff --git a/android/src/main/java/expo/modules/widgets/notifications/CustomNotificationBuilder.kt b/android/src/main/java/expo/modules/widgets/notifications/CustomNotificationBuilder.kt
